# Project Structure Guardrails

- Keep public library source in `src/`: components in `src/components/<ComponentName>/`, package entrypoint in `src/test-stpr-ui-kit.ts`.
- Keep Storybook stories in `src/stories/<ComponentName>/<ComponentName>.stories.tsx`.
- Keep Storybook and developer docs in `src/documentation/`:
  - product intro and user-facing docs in `src/documentation/*.mdx`;
  - process docs in `src/documentation/development/*.mdx`;
  - short how-to references in `src/documentation/cheatSheets/*.mdx`.
- Keep shared Storybook/demo helpers in `src/hooks`, `src/utils`, `src/styles`, and media assets in `src/images`.
- Keep Storybook-only static fixtures and demo images in `src/story-assets/` (served via `.storybook/main.ts` `staticDirs`); keep static files shipped with the library (fallback images, IFC wasm, etc.) under `public/components-assets/<Component>/…` (copied into `dist/` by Vite `copyPublicDir`).
- Keep Storybook runtime config in `.storybook/`; do not place component business logic there.
- Keep automation/build helpers in `scripts/` and project-level editor/agent config in `.cursor/`.
- Treat `dist/` and `storybook-static/` as generated output; do not place source-of-truth code there.
- For any new feature touching component API, align all affected layers:
  1) `src/components`;
  2) `src/test-stpr-ui-kit.ts`;
  3) `src/stories`;
  4) `src/documentation` and `CHANGELOG.md`.
- Avoid creating alternative top-level source folders when an existing canonical folder already fits the change.
